meta {
  name: saveEtimClassification
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: https://{{customer}}.{{domain}}/jsonrpc
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "method": "saveEtimClassification",
    "params": {
      "product_id": 123,
      "etim_class_type": "REGULAR",
      "etim_release": "ETIM-10.0",
      "etim_class_code": "EC002713",
      "etim_class_version": 10
    },
    "id": 1
  }
}

docs {
  Set or change the ETIM classification for a product. If the ETIM class code changes, all existing feature values for that product/type/release are removed.

  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `product_id` | integer (nullable) | no | Internal product ID; required unless external_product_id is supplied |
  | `external_product_id` | string (nullable) | no | External product ID; required unless product_id is supplied |
  | `etim_class_type` | string | no | ETIM class type: REGULAR or MODELLING |
  | `etim_release` | string | no | ETIM release (e.g. "ETIM-9.0"). Use "DYNAMIC" for MODELLING type only |
  | `etim_class_code` | string (nullable) | no | ETIM class code to assign (e.g. "EC000001"); omit to keep the current class |
  | `etim_class_version` | integer (nullable) | no | Specific ETIM class version to pin; omit to use the latest version for the given release |

  **Example: Assign REGULAR classification**. Class version is optional; omit it to use the latest version for the release.

  ```json
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "method": "saveEtimClassification",
    "params": {
      "product_id": 123,
      "etim_class_type": "REGULAR",
      "etim_release": "ETIM-10.0",
      "etim_class_code": "EC002713",
      "etim_class_version": 10
    },
    "id": 1
  }
  ```

  Result:

  ```json
  {
    "product_id": 123,
    "etim_class_type": "REGULAR",
    "etim_release": "ETIM-10.0",
    "etim_class_code": "EC002713",
    "etim_class_version": 10
  }
  ```
}
